join detective right
detective: The others report that Dracula collapsed shortly after consuming a dessert that you prepared.
detective (thinking): The behavior exhibited by Dracula is characteristic of vampiric garlic poisoning.
detective (speaking): You didn't happen to let garlic into Dracula's dessert, did you?
join cook left
cook: Of course not. I'm a chef for a vampire household. Garlic stays far, far away from here.
detective: Would you mind if I searched the cabinets?
cook: Not at all. Take a look, only vampire-safe ingredients in there.
[style name="dialogue_style"]
You search the cabinet. There isn't any garlic in sight.
cook: See? I might not be his biggest fan, but I mean him no harm.
